From 8999dc809f8060fa8ba5d697bb76c478bd54841e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:44:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ADD route selected-agent slash commands through backend
 hooks

Selected-agent slash-prefixed messages use a provider command hook so backend commands such as Codex status and fork actions are handled without entering the normal model prompt or orchestrator directive path. The provider contract documents the optional hook and keeps unsupported commands visible without sending a model turn.
---
 docs/architecture.md  |  17 +++++--
 src/agent_runtime.rs  |  17 ++++++-
 src/cli.rs            |  31 +++++++++++-
 src/codex.rs          |  31 ++++++++++++
 src/workspace.rs      | 114 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/terminal_app.rs |  33 ++++++++++--
 tests/workspace.rs    |  52 +++++++++++++++----
 7 files changed, 273 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index e319204..2d12ef4 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -170,6 +170,9 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` handles provider-owned slash commands for an existing session without
+  sending them through the normal model prompt path. The default implementation returns a visible
+  unsupported-command reply so providers can ignore backend commands safely.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
@@ -652,17 +655,21 @@ New agent-provider support follows this path:
 1. Define an `AgentProfile` with `AgentKind::External`.
 2. Implement `AgentBackend` for the provider.
 3. Override streaming methods when the provider can emit real-time output.
-4. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
-5. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
-6. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
+4. Override `AgentBackend::command` when the provider exposes session-local slash commands that
+   should not become model prompts.
+5. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
+6. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
+7. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
 
 `AgentBackend::session` is an optional session snapshot hook. Work Leaf tracks hidden system-agent
 initialization itself, so provider implementations do not need to override `session` for persistent
-`command-agent` or `title-agent` turns to use launch once and send thereafter.
+`command-agent` or `title-agent` turns to use launch once and send thereafter. Backend command
+handling is also optional; providers that do not expose slash-command actions keep the default
+unsupported-command response.
 
 New core workflow behavior belongs in the workflow module that owns the behavior. UI adapters should
 only translate user input into controller calls and render controller snapshots. Agent providers
-should only implement launch, send, streaming, and shutdown behavior.
+should only implement launch, send, backend command, streaming, and shutdown behavior.
 
 ## API and Architecture Change Policy
 
